WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.980
<b><i>We look the same, but men call us monsters. 

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.220
Joujin!

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.600
Let me inside the Murakumo.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.210
Kouga Hachirou is here!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:56.050
<b><i>100 Eyes See Their Destiny</i></b>

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.830
Kujaku Tsuibamu...

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.330
Namenba, hold a funeral for Gorone!

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.480
We're going inside, too.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.040
I'll go see what's going 
on around him, again.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.370
Saizou, watch from above.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.670
Let's go, Shikibu.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.610
Yeah.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.410
We'll save Hachirou and Hibiki.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.290
Then, I'll go around to the rear.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.260
You, too!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.190
<i>It's too narrow.</i>

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.310
<i>That rubbery monk could 
probably get in, but...</i>

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:39.590
Your guts will burst out and fall to the 
ground, and you will go to hell.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.470
Yasha Itaru.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.250
Is that...

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:38.150
It can't be. Destiny's Passage?

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.150
Let's hear all you know

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.900
about the Joujinshuu's techniques.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:48.160
It shares its name with the power 
possessed by Gautama Buddha.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.910
But the technique itself

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:57.710
shows its victim their whole life, 
making it seem to be a great evil.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.920
<i>The whole world comes down 
to the roll of the dice.</i>

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.440
<i>They roll and roll on the mat.</i>

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.180
<i>You dream and dream. And at the end,</i>

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.070
<i>you will eventually die.</i>

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:16.440
Listen, to play Kachi Kachi, 
you add up the two cards.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.940
Whoever has the higher first 
digit of the total, wins.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.440
Okay, how many points is this?

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.700
I guess it's still too soon for this...

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.700
Six.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:34.450
Five.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.330
Eight.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.340
Two sevens.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:51.860
<i>Dad... How long are we going to do this?</i>

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:52.970
<i>Dad.</i>

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.130
I've never seen you before.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.230
Yeah, I travel around...

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.150
You got any money?

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.700
Just a little...

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.740
Let us see.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.690
Okay, next round!

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.390
I win.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:27.490
Damn it!

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:28.510
I'm staying in.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:31.850
What's wrong?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.390
Give me just a second.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.890
We don't have all night.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.650
Six. Five.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.910
Two sevens.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.660
Sometimes, a man's gotta take a risk!

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:00.780
Six!

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.570
Five.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.430
Two sevens...

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:06.170
Crap!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:11.170
<i>You guys are being played for fools.</i>

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.930
<i>Yeah, so am I, of course.</i>

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.640
<i>No...</i>

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.940
<i>I bet he was being played, too.</i>

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.770
Tadanaga-sama...

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.720
Welcome, Kouga Hachirou.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.320
Joujin...

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:01.850
Where's Hibiki?

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.250
I want her back.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:10.860
Did you think you could get 
our Ouka by doing this?

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:12.900
No.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.550
My wish was never for the Ouka.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.770
Listen, Hachirou!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:22.370
Do you think the world is at peace now?

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:26.890
You say nothing, eh?

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.400
Of course not.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.880
Why did your mother and 
father die so horribly,

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.880
if the world is at peace?

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.720
It was because of the Tokugawas!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.220
The Tokugawas?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.170
That's just what I hoped you would say.

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:46.900
The temporary peace the Tokugawas created...

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:53.030
Hachirou, the civil wars never ended!

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.340
They aren't over.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.160
There hasn't been enough killing!

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.520
What are you talking about?

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:03.660
Should that hell on Earth really be 
allowed to end in such a neat fashion?

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.570
Don't you understand 
Joujin-sama's compassion?

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:10.420
His compassion that equals the Buddha's.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.230
Bullshit!

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:15.060
The Buddha wishes to save the world.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:17.380
You are the evil passions of the civil wars.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.680
The exact opposite!

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.700
You see, I want to bring true salvation.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.580
And to do that,

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:31.690
the people of this world must 
experience a bit of hell.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.260
The sinners... The innocent...

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.550
Both of them will burn.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:42.940
And when none who long for war, 
even in the slightest, are left,

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:47.160
that will be true salvation, true peace.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.620
And that is my real wish.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:52.040
What?

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.470
The Tokugawas...

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:56.320
The Tokugawas, who would 
create a temporary peace

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:00.280
and then engage in that childish game 
to determine the next heir...

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.590
You think they can do that?

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.100
Thus, my desire...

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:12.520
My desire for a great demon king, who can 
wield the sword that summons demons!

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:33.790
Five. Sorry.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.670
Cheater! You're cheating... I know it!

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.430
Hey, now...

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.180
Don't take it out on me, 
just because you keep losing.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:46.680
But after all the money 
we've lost to an outsider,

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.740
I can understand how he feels.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:52.920
Anyway, let's all have fun.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.970
<i>As long as Saizou's eye is on the ceiling,</i>

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:01.850
<i>you can never win.</i>

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.960
Dad, it's cold...

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.910
Oh, I win again?

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.460
Today's my lucky day.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:20.820
<i>Saizou, this is the last round for today...</i>

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:22.370
<i>Don't screw it up.</i>

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:24.830
<i>Once we're done, I'll get you 
something warm to eat.</i>

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.110
One more card.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.630
I won't lose this time.

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:42.610
I'm in.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:46.120
Yeah, I guess I'll get in, too.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:50.740
<i>A three and a six, huh? 
That's a good hand...</i>

00:12:56.510 --> 00:12:58.750
<i>What's that idiot doing?!</i>

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.600
Okay, in or out?

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.200
Add up your cards, and the first 
digit closest to nine wins.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.770
But matching cards beat it.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.440
I'm not letting some outsider beat me!

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:24.400
<i>Look at this hand...</i>

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.660
<i>Lady Luck really is with me today.</i>

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:30.190
<i>I can win on my own!</i>

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:33.910
It's the last round, so I'll 
bet everything I've got!

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.900
I'm in.

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:38.420
I'm out.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.420
Me, too.

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:43.420
Okay, winner takes all, then.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.490
Let's see 'em!

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:48.830
I've got a three and a six!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.110
Doubles!

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:53.860
And that's matching tens, the strongest hand.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.150
You win double!

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:56.520
Wow!

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.300
We took everything you had, huh?

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:05.440
What were you doing?!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:08.950
The Moon...

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.580
What about the Moon?

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.560
You little shit...

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.940
I didn't mean to. I didn't...

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.200
<i>I did it deliberately.</i>

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:27.590
<i>I wanted all this crap to end.</i>

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:31.130
<i>It was supposed to end here...</i>

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.260
<i>Right here.</i>

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.190
<i>It was supposed to end.</i>

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.400
<i>If the Kouga hadn't taken me in...</i>

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:01.640
After you peer into the abyss of despair,

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.740
Yasha's words bring you to your doom.

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:08.250
<i>My leader...</i>

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:12.510
<i>I didn't care about you, either.</i>

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.750
Their destiny is to fall,

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:23.910
but the cherry blossoms always return.

00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:27.280
So, everyone, like cherry blossoms,

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.030
I command you to fall!

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.280
Go to hell!

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.810
<i>That was always the plan.</i>

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:48.050
<i>That's a perfect way to scatter 
my guts on the ground...</i>

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:28.270
<i>But...</i>

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.680
<i>I'm kind of an asshole, you see.</i>

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:36.850
<i>And I don't like doing things, 
just because I'm told to!</i>

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:41.330
Saizou!

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:45.350
What are you doing, Saizou?!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.280
I already see too much.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:06.230
So as a rule,

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:09.030
I don't look at things I don't need to see.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:12.530
I can't see what I want to see.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.400
So my dreams have only been terrible.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:21.640
This is probably the prettiest thing 
I've ever seen in this world.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:01.690
Saizou!

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:09.710
It stopped.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:13.960
Who cares if you stopped the Murakumo?

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:19.400
Did you think this was a 
palanquin to carry us to Edo?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:26.060
The Murakumo is not simply a moving castle.

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:33.920
It is a barrier which enables the secret 
ritual to revive Lord Nobunaga.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.930
Not only that,

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.650
but when he revives,

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:43.470
when he is born as a child... no, as a beast,

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:49.060
the Murakumo is the womb which will 
awaken the memories within him.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.810
And his desire for glory!

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.920
That's a wonderful speech.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:59.080
You should make this dream 
of yours into a Noh play.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:03.200
But I have no intention 
of playing a part in it!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.140
No, no.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.990
You must play your role.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:09.330
You...

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:12.210
And Hibiki!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.220
And Hibiki?

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:17.570
Indeed.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.480
She is a necessary aspect 
of the revival ritual.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:25.470
What do Hibiki and I have to do with this?

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.870
You're an irreplaceable piece of the puzzle,

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:31.670
a young man and woman 
in love with each other.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:35.050
Of course, not just any man and woman.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:38.470
The two must be of a worthy bloodline,

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:42.930
masters of an art, with perfect 
bodies and strong souls!

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.620
For what?

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:48.370
The two of you must lie together.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:55.470
The fluids of your coupling 
will pour into the skull,

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.750
becoming the blood connecting it to a body.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:04.660
Only then will the great 
demon king be reborn!

00:20:05.110 --> 00:20:07.880
And you think we'll agree to this?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.550
Will you not?

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.080
You know the answer!

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:17.780
Then, you and Hibiki must kill each other.

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:22.180
You and she must try to kill the other!

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:24.030
What?

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:26.110
Know this, Hachirou.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:28.890
The fluids born of love

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:32.790
are the same as the blood that 
flows in deadly combat!

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:37.170
If I cannot have those fluids, 
I shall need blood instead!

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.240
Nonsense...

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:42.020
We will not lie together.

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:43.680
Let alone kill each other!

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:47.570
You will have no choice.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.230
Hibiki!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:04.950
What? Hibiki?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:07.700
Hibiki?

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.350
I am Oboro of Iga.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:15.460
Have you forgotten me, Kouga Gennosuke-sama?

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:19.330
No, Kouga Gennosuke!

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:24.120
If only I'd never made the mistake 
of falling in love with you,

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:28.790
they wouldn't... They wouldn't have died!

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.180
I can never regret it enough.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.480
I can never apologize enough.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:38.230
I must, at least, offer my 
head before their graves!

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:41.150
No, that isn't enough... It isn't enough!

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.990
First, Gennosuke, I must 
offer them your head!

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:27.050
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:30.800
No... You're the monster.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:38.310
I'm about to change that 
disgusting fate of yours.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:38.560
<b><i>We Must See the Lotus Flowers Together</i></b>
